question:
In SCSS, what is the computed specificity of this nested rule?
```scss
.parent {
  .child { color: blue; }
}
```

How do mixins and functions differ in SCSS?
```scss
@mixin border-radius($radius) { border-radius: $radius; }
@function calc-width($base) { @return $base * 2; }
```

What is the variable scope in this SCSS?
```scss
.parent {
  $color: blue;
  .child { color: $color; }
}
.sibling { color: $color; } /* error? */
```

When should @extend be avoided in favor of mixins?
```scss
.base { color: blue; margin: 10px; }
.derived { @extend .base; padding: 5px; }
```

What will this SCSS map iteration compile to?
```scss
$colors: (primary: blue, secondary: gray);
@each $name, $value in $colors {
  .btn-#{$name} { color: $value; }
}
```

How does the parent selector (&) work in nested pseudo-classes?
```scss
button {
  &:hover { color: red; }
  &::before { content: 'icon'; }
}
```

What does this preprocessor compilation reveal about file organization?
```scss
@import 'variables';
@import 'mixins';
@import 'components';
```

Why might deep nesting in SCSS cause specificity creep?
```scss
.outer {
  .middle {
    .inner {
      p { color: blue; }
    }
  }
}
```

What is the output when using a preprocessor function in a property?
```scss
$base-size: 16px;
.text { font-size: calc($base-size * 1.5); }
```

When should CSS custom properties (variables) be preferred over preprocessor variables?
```css
:root { --color: blue; }
@media (dark) { --color: darkblue; }
```
